// Title: PortProxy registry rule creation (netsh portproxy ground truth)
// MITRE: T1090.001 (Internal Proxy), T1112 (Modify Registry)
// Data sources: DeviceRegistryEvents
// False positive notes: Near-zero. Anything writing a PortProxy v*tov* value without a
//                       corresponding sysadmin change ticket is suspicious. Load-balancer
//                       admins occasionally script portproxy; allow-list those hosts.
// Tested against: Synthetic DeviceRegistryEvents; CISA AA24-038A IOC layout.
// Author: detection pack maintainers
// Date: 2026-06-27
//
// CISA AA24-038A: Volt Typhoon used netsh to create a PortProxy registry modification
// [T1112] on a PRTG server, converting it into a relay for C2 [T1090.001]. The OS writes
// this key as a side effect of `netsh interface portproxy add` regardless of how netsh was
// invoked. Even if the command line is encoded/obfuscated and never logs the word
// "portproxy", this key is written. That makes it the artifact the operator cannot hide.
//
// Note on the key path: Defender/Sysmon log the live control set (e.g. ControlSet001),
// not the CurrentControlSet symlink, so this matches on the \Services\PortProxy\ substring
// to catch ControlSet001/002/CurrentControlSet alike, and all four address-family variants.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where Timestamp > ago(30d)
| where RegistryKey has @"\Services\PortProxy\"
| where RegistryKey has_any (@"\v4tov4", @"\v4tov6", @"\v6tov4", @"\v6tov6")
| where ActionType in ("RegistryValueSet", "RegistryKeyCreated")
//
// In v4tov4\tcp the value NAME encodes listen address/port and the value DATA encodes the
// forward (connect) address/port: e.g. name "0.0.0.0/9999" data "192.0.2.10/8443".
| extend ListenAddress = tostring(extract(@"^(.+?)/\d+$", 1, RegistryValueName))
| extend ListenPort    = tostring(extract(@"/(\d+)$", 1, RegistryValueName))
| extend ForwardInfo   = RegistryValueData
//
| extend IsAllInterfaces   = ListenAddress in ("0.0.0.0", "::", "*")
| extend ForwardsToPrivate = RegistryValueData matches regex @"(^|/)(10\.|192\.168\.|172\.(1[6-9]|2[0-9]|3[01])\.)"
| extend Severity = case(
    IsAllInterfaces and ForwardsToPrivate, "Critical",
    IsAllInterfaces,                        "High",
    "Medium")
| extend Phase = "C2-PortProxy-Registry"
| project Timestamp, DeviceName, Severity, ActionType, RegistryKey, RegistryValueName,
          RegistryValueData, ListenAddress, ListenPort, ForwardInfo,
          IsAllInterfaces, ForwardsToPrivate,
          InitiatingProcessAccountName, InitiatingProcessFileName,
          InitiatingProcessCommandLine, Phase
| order by Timestamp desc
